# Redesigned 2026-08-31 (owner spec): a path PORTION that REACHES a filesystem
# sink is the finding. Absolute and relative both count; a literal nothing opens
# does not; a bare filename is allowed; anything computed is clean.
#
# The negatives are load-bearing: with only the two positives this file would
# pass against the OLD unscoped rule, which fired on every drive-letter literal.
hardcoded-absolute-path 16
hardcoded-absolute-path 18
!hardcoded-absolute-path 21
!hardcoded-absolute-path 24
!hardcoded-absolute-path 26
